.SH FILES
.na
.nh
.TP
\fI/var/lib/otpme/tree/\fR
The objects of the realm, on the nodes and, by sync, on the hosts.
A group is the directory \fI<group>.group\fR in the directory of its unit, e.g. \fI<realm>.realm/<site>.site/groups.unit/developers.group/\fR, with its settings in \fIobject.json\fR.
Change them with the commands above, not in the file.
.TP
\fI/var/cache/otpme/nsscache/group.cache\fR
The groups with their \fBgidNumber\fR and \fBmemberUid\fR, as NSS reads them on a host or node.
\fI/etc/group.cache\fR points to it.
.hy
.ad
